{
  "$comment": [
    "Arm definitions for the repeatable performance matrix (.github/workflows/perf-matrix.yml).",
    "SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH: the workflow derives its matrix from this file and hardcodes nothing.",
    "",
    "ROUND 2 - CORRECTED SLICING MATRIX (#1017).",
    "",
    "Round 1 ran only SHARD 1 of each split and multiplied by N to estimate total work.",
    "That is invalid: vitest shards by FILE COUNT, not duration, and 13 of 205 files carry",
    "~89% of the work - so shard 1 of 8 drew light files (0.80 min) while shard 1 of 4 drew",
    "heavy ones (1.90 min), and N x T did not conserve total work. EVERY shard of every",
    "split is now an arm, so the split is measured rather than extrapolated from one slice.",
    "",
    "Arms carrying `shardGroup` are aggregated by the collator: SUM across the group is the",
    "runner-minutes cost, MAX is the wall-clock cost. Reporting only one of those is how a",
    "sharding decision gets made on the wrong axis.",
    "",
    "Round 1 also created FOUR byte-identical arms by accident (fast-nocov == slice-fast-2",
    "== lever-baseline == lever-control). That was wasteful but informative: 20 samples of",
    "one configuration put the noise floor at ~14%, well above the 9% the power analysis",
    "assumed. Nothing below ~15-20% is readable from this harness. perf-plan.mjs now fails",
    "on undeclared duplicates.",
    "",
    "The coverage-provider and per-lever arms are NOT repeated here - round 1 is still",
    "running them on its own ref, and repeating them would confound two rounds."
  ],
  "defaultRepetitions": 3,
